WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Downloaded from
YTS.MX

2
00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:10.594
[gentle piano music]

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Official YIFY movies site:
YTS.MX

4
00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:17.726
[inaudible]

5
00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.567
[audience cheering]

6
00:00:25.651 --> 00:00:28.445
[piano music grows warmer]

7
00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:46.672
[Shawn Mendes] You first get on the stage,
and ego comes rushing in.

8
00:00:49.341 --> 00:00:51.510
And it goes, "Don't mess up,

9
00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:54.137
'cause you're the man.

10
00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:57.224
Everyone's saying you're the man,
so don't mess up."

11
00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.810
So you get to the mic,
and your first note is flat.

12
00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.228
[chuckles] Always.

13
00:01:04.856 --> 00:01:07.067
And then about 30 seconds in, you go...

14
00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:10.904
"Oh, yeah, 
I'm just a guy and I love music."

15
00:01:10.988 --> 00:01:12.948
And your whole body releases.

16
00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.869
And I just let go
and I look around, and I'm just like...

17
00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:20.998
"Just do this.

18
00:01:21.707 --> 00:01:22.708
Drop the ego.

19
00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:26.670
Time to surrender."

20
00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.631
[audience cheering]

21
00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:32.384
[shower running]

22
00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.773
[warm music creeping in]

23
00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:07.711
[typing on phone]

24
00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:11.340
[automated female voice]
Ever since I was about ten years old,

25
00:02:11.423 --> 00:02:14.718
I was obsessed 
with being really good at things.

26
00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.511
[typing on phone]

27
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.934
That my worth is based on what I do.

28
00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:26.688
And that can lead to a dark place.

29
00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:27.856
[typing on phone]

30
00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:34.988
My voice hit its breaking point
at the end of this tour,

31
00:02:35.072 --> 00:02:37.741
-and I'm using my phone to talk.
-[playing melody]

32
00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:42.954
Last night reminded me...

33
00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.957
I'm not invincible.

34
00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:51.254
[audience cheering]

35
00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.007
[Shawn playing "Use Somebody"]

36
00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.725
♪ Say whoa-oh-oh ♪

37
00:03:03.809 --> 00:03:04.643
Sing!

38
00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.395
[audience] ♪ Whoa-oh-oh ♪

39
00:03:06.478 --> 00:03:08.188
♪ Say whoa-oh-oh ♪

40
00:03:08.271 --> 00:03:09.147
Louder!

41
00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:10.941
[audience] ♪ Whoa-oh-oh ♪

42
00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.651
♪ Say yeah ♪

43
00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:13.568
Scream it!

44
00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:15.362
-[stamps foot]
-[audience] ♪ Yeah ♪

45
00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:17.447
♪ Now oh-oh-oh
Oh, yeah ♪

46
00:03:17.531 --> 00:03:19.741
-[stamping foot]
-[audience clapping]

47
00:03:20.283 --> 00:03:23.370
No matter how fast I get,
do not stop clapping, all right?

48
00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:26.164
Here we go! Clap those hands! Clap!

49
00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:28.375
[audience clapping]

50
00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:30.836
Faster!

51
00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:33.338
[clapping and music accelerate]

52
00:03:37.592 --> 00:03:38.427
Faster!

53
00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:45.684
Faster!

54
00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.145
[audience cheering loudly]

55
00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:13.879
-[plays slowly]
-[audience cheering]

56
00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:29.060
[gentle instrumental music]

57
00:04:30.353 --> 00:04:32.355
[audience cheering loudly]

58
00:04:43.366 --> 00:04:46.036
-[man] Hey, uh, good one.
-[Shawn] Thank you, brother.

59
00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.499
Give us a hug.

60
00:04:52.793 --> 00:04:55.462
[indistinct chatter]

61
00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:59.925
-Thank you so much.
-[man 1] Let's go. Let's motor up.

62
00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:03.178
-We've got an interview outside.
-[man 2] I'm not done with it.

63
00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:07.182
[woman] You're gonna make a left
when you come out

64
00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:08.683
and go through the lights.

65
00:05:14.689 --> 00:05:17.567
-[Shawn] Thank you. Thank you.
-[woman 1] Bye!

66
00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:20.403
[woman 2] I love you! I love you!

67
00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:29.996
-[objects clattering]
-[man 1] Right there.

68
00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.082
A little further. Right there.

69
00:05:38.713 --> 00:05:41.383
[man 2] Just keep an eye...
I can't see the monitor...

70
00:05:41.466 --> 00:05:43.343
So just keep an eye on the recording.

71
00:05:43.426 --> 00:05:47.097
[softly] ♪ Oh, no, there it goes
Start another fire ♪

72
00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:49.933
♪ Baby, oh, no, no ♪

73
00:05:50.851 --> 00:05:56.815
[vocalizing a scale]

74
00:05:57.691 --> 00:06:01.778
Hey, Cez, Jocelyn's gonna come.
I told her to be here for 11:50.

75
00:06:03.572 --> 00:06:04.781
[man] All right.

76
00:06:05.407 --> 00:06:08.952
[male interviewer] So, this thing
you start doing in your bedroom,

77
00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.787
making Vines for the love of it...

78
00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.748
Is it hard to protect
that pure thing that started it all?

79
00:06:16.418 --> 00:06:18.086
[exhales deeply]

80
00:06:21.715 --> 00:06:24.384
[gentle piano music]

81
00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:33.018
[Karen Mendes] Come on, Shawn, let's go!
Time to go in!

82
00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:35.270
Get up.

83
00:06:40.775 --> 00:06:44.779
[Shawn] As a kid, when you look at someone
and you're like, "This is my dream..."

84
00:06:44.863 --> 00:06:47.324
And someone goes, "That's a stupid dream,"

85
00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.868
you'd be like,
"Oh, yeah, it is a stupid dream."

86
00:06:51.828 --> 00:06:53.955
When I got into school...

87
00:06:55.624 --> 00:06:59.127
Ms. Parker,
she was the vocal class teacher,

88
00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:01.212
and I told her, "I want to be a singer.

89
00:07:01.296 --> 00:07:04.507
I want to be...
I want to be an artist." You know?

90
00:07:06.635 --> 00:07:08.928
And she had no hesitation to believe me.

91
00:07:10.722 --> 00:07:12.515
My parents, my friends...

92
00:07:12.599 --> 00:07:14.935
Nobody looked at me and said, 
"You're crazy."

93
00:07:15.018 --> 00:07:17.312
Everybody was like, "Go for it."

94
00:07:17.896 --> 00:07:18.980
[strumming melody]

95
00:07:19.064 --> 00:07:21.191
[Manny] He sounds better
all the time now.

96
00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:23.109
With more practice like he's had...

97
00:07:23.193 --> 00:07:24.527
[Karen] Hey!

98
00:07:24.611 --> 00:07:26.988
-We love you, Shawn Mendes!
-I'm excited!

99
00:07:27.072 --> 00:07:29.074
[indistinct conversation]

100
00:07:29.658 --> 00:07:31.618
[Manny] This is larger than I thought.

101
00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:32.535
[man] Yeah.

102
00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:35.622
-[man] Can he hear it?
-No. No, no. Nothing can be heard.

103
00:07:35.705 --> 00:07:38.541
[Manny] He may not like being filmed.
He's saying hello.

104
00:07:38.625 --> 00:07:40.835
-Hi.
-[Shawn] He can't be filmed.

105
00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:43.546
-[Manny] This ain't going anywhere.
-Okay.

106
00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:44.631
Hey, Mom?

107
00:07:46.758 --> 00:07:47.801
What do you say now?

108
00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.844
It is nuts.

109
00:07:51.721 --> 00:07:54.933
What, even to go to the bathroom,
he has to go with security.

110
00:07:55.642 --> 00:07:57.644
-[woman] Oh, my God!
-[women screaming]

111
00:07:57.727 --> 00:07:58.895
[woman] Oh, my God!

112
00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.313
Oh, my God!

113
00:08:00.855 --> 00:08:02.232
I love you!

114
00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:03.566
[Manny] Did you see that?

115
00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:05.860
-"I love you"? Holy moly.
-[Karen laughs]

116
00:08:07.028 --> 00:08:09.030
[women cheering] Hi!

117
00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:14.285
-You're not embarrassed of what?
-I'm nervous now.

118
00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:15.829
I wasn't nervous until now.

119
00:08:17.288 --> 00:08:18.498
Can we go back there?

120
00:08:18.581 --> 00:08:20.583
[Manny] Hold on. Stay with me.

121
00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:23.920
-[man] Give it up for Shawn Mendes!
-[audience cheering]

122
00:08:26.715 --> 00:08:28.717
[Shawn playing "Give Me Love"]

123
00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.927
♪ Give a little time to me ♪

124
00:08:31.803 --> 00:08:33.430
♪ We'll burn this out ♪

125
00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:36.266
♪ We'll play hide and seek ♪

126
00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:37.892
♪ To turn this around ♪

127
00:08:37.976 --> 00:08:42.272
♪ Oh, what I want is the taste
That your lips allow ♪

128
00:08:42.355 --> 00:08:44.941
Do I have anyone from outside of Ontario?

129
00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:47.527
-Where are you guys from?
-Michigan.

130
00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.987
Michigan!

131
00:08:49.070 --> 00:08:50.488
Holy...

132
00:08:51.406 --> 00:08:52.407
Crazy.

133
00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.702
[playing "Say Something"]

134
00:08:55.785 --> 00:08:59.831
♪ Say something
I'm giving up on you ♪

135
00:09:00.915 --> 00:09:05.462
I think I'd heard A Great Big World,
"Say Something" for the first time,

136
00:09:05.545 --> 00:09:08.256
and I was like,
"Wow, that's a really great song."

137
00:09:08.339 --> 00:09:09.174
Googled it...

138
00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:14.220
and one of the first search results
was Shawn's cover of the song.

139
00:09:14.304 --> 00:09:15.555
[playing "Say Something"]

140
00:09:15.638 --> 00:09:19.976
♪ Say something
I'm giving up on you ♪

141
00:09:20.435 --> 00:09:24.314
[Gertler] I was taken aback a bit.
It was like, "This is really incredible."

142
00:09:26.191 --> 00:09:29.986
Reached out,
and we FaceTimed Shawn and his mom.

143
00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:33.740
Immediately, Shawn just starts
grilling us with questions

144
00:09:33.823 --> 00:09:37.952
about how the music business works,
why he might need a manager.

145
00:09:38.036 --> 00:09:39.746
I just said to them,
I was honest,

146
00:09:39.829 --> 00:09:42.499
"I don't know everything,
but I'm going to sit here

147
00:09:42.582 --> 00:09:45.919
and spend every minute of my time
figuring it out with you."

148
00:09:47.629 --> 00:09:51.174
[Shawn] I would always say to him,
"I need to get a band

149
00:09:51.257 --> 00:09:53.843
'cause I'll sound bad on my own,"
and he'd say, "No.

150
00:09:53.927 --> 00:09:56.346
Just get on the stage,
just you and the guitar."

151
00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:57.972
Having the confidence

152
00:09:58.056 --> 00:10:02.101
was all based off of those first couple
years of performing with just a guitar.

153
00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:08.441
I went from a small bedroom in Pickering

154
00:10:08.525 --> 00:10:11.986
to playing in front of a few
thousand people in a couple years.

155
00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:15.156
[singing indistinctly]

156
00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:18.660
-[audience cheering]
-[electric guitar chords resonating]

157
00:10:31.214 --> 00:10:33.550
[Shawn playing
"I Wanna Dance with Somebody"]

158
00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:35.760
♪ I wanna dance with somebody ♪

159
00:10:35.844 --> 00:10:38.930
♪ I wanna feel the heat with somebody ♪

160
00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:42.767
♪ Yeah! I wanna dance with somebody ♪

161
00:10:42.851 --> 00:10:46.229
♪ With somebody who loves me
Yeah ♪

162
00:10:46.312 --> 00:10:49.524
♪ Oh, I wanna dance with somebody ♪

163
00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:53.820
♪ I wanna feel the heat with somebody
Yeah ♪

164
00:10:53.903 --> 00:10:56.406
♪ Oh! I wanna dance with somebody ♪

165
00:10:57.866 --> 00:11:00.577
♪ With somebody who loves me ♪

166
00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:05.164
It looks so cool.

167
00:11:06.833 --> 00:11:09.335
This is what it's like
filming a documentary.

168
00:11:09.419 --> 00:11:10.295
Here we go.

169
00:11:11.129 --> 00:11:15.800
-[playing melody]
-[indistinct conversation]

170
00:11:16.384 --> 00:11:18.344
I'm not ready to give this to Scott.

171
00:11:19.178 --> 00:11:20.263
[man] He's not here.

172
00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:23.975
It all stems from when I met him,
and he had these cool sunglasses on.

173
00:11:24.058 --> 00:11:27.270
He said, "If you had a number one single,
I'll give them to you."

174
00:11:27.353 --> 00:11:29.731
The first thing we did together
went number one.

175
00:11:29.814 --> 00:11:31.149
It needs another melody.

176
00:11:31.232 --> 00:11:32.859
Yeah, it's just, like...

177
00:11:32.942 --> 00:11:34.652
♪ You say... ♪

178
00:11:34.736 --> 00:11:38.615
[playing melody]

179
00:11:42.785 --> 00:11:43.745
How's that?

180
00:11:44.329 --> 00:11:49.292
♪ I don't wanna see my lie ♪

181
00:11:49.375 --> 00:11:50.627
[Scott] Got it?

182
00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.254
[vocalizing]
♪ ...my eyes ♪

183
00:11:54.464 --> 00:11:56.174
♪ So I say that ♪

184
00:11:56.257 --> 00:12:00.887
♪ I don't wanna see you cry ♪

185
00:12:02.138 --> 00:12:06.851
[vocalizing]

186
00:12:08.311 --> 00:12:09.812
In my room, there's this thing

187
00:12:09.896 --> 00:12:12.857
that has the number of shows
that we're on and where we are.

188
00:12:12.941 --> 00:12:14.901
Today it's at number eight, Copenhagen,

189
00:12:14.984 --> 00:12:17.445
and it made me think
we're not even close to 100.

190
00:12:17.528 --> 00:12:18.780
[man laughs]

191
00:12:18.863 --> 00:12:20.949
But it also said Cologne, not Copenhagen.

192
00:12:21.032 --> 00:12:23.201
-We're in Cologne.
-[Shawn] It said Cologne.

193
00:12:23.284 --> 00:12:26.621
-Actually, it might have said Copenhagen.
-[all laughing]

194
00:12:26.704 --> 00:12:29.958
But I want us to always
keep in mind that this is very special.

195
00:12:30.041 --> 00:12:32.001
I'll say it, I know it'll get annoying,

196
00:12:32.085 --> 00:12:34.921
but it truly is so special.
What we get to do is magical.

197
00:12:35.004 --> 00:12:37.507
Everyone in there,
it's their first time seeing it,

198
00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:38.591
every single time.

199
00:12:38.675 --> 00:12:41.344
-No matter if it's show one or show 99.
-That's right.

200
00:12:41.427 --> 00:12:44.889
It's their first time seeing it,
it's special, so thanks. Let's do it.

201
00:12:44.973 --> 00:12:46.516
-Beautiful.
-Let's do it.

202
00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:48.309
Everybody jump!

203
00:12:48.393 --> 00:12:50.853
[audience singing indistinctly to music] 

204
00:12:59.612 --> 00:13:02.490
[Shawn] I used to look
at so many of my idols and be like,

205
00:13:02.573 --> 00:13:04.701
"How can you ever be that?

206
00:13:06.369 --> 00:13:08.871
They were born legendary."

207
00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:12.667
That's just not the truth.

208
00:13:15.003 --> 00:13:17.005
[audience cheering]

209
00:13:21.718 --> 00:13:25.596
[Shawn] People are like, "What would you
be doing if this didn't happen?"

210
00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.141
I feel puzzled by that question,

211
00:13:28.891 --> 00:13:31.394
because I feel like
this is what I was going to do.

212
00:13:33.062 --> 00:13:34.856
I'm in the Q&A yesterday.

213
00:13:35.606 --> 00:13:38.860
This girl goes,
"How do I be a songwriter like you?"

214
00:13:39.694 --> 00:13:42.155
I immediately
thought about saying that to my dad,

215
00:13:42.238 --> 00:13:45.116
"I wanna be a songwriter."
He goes, "Can you write songs?"

216
00:13:45.199 --> 00:13:47.410
I said, "I don't know."
He goes, "Write one."

217
00:13:49.996 --> 00:13:52.790
I sat in my room
and I played guitar for seven hours.

218
00:13:52.874 --> 00:13:56.127
My hands bled. I'd play again 
and get better, and I'd practice.

219
00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:59.922
And I'm not saying everyone has to be
so Olympic athlete about it.

220
00:14:00.006 --> 00:14:03.551
I said that to her. I was like,
"Stop sitting here thinking about it.

221
00:14:04.052 --> 00:14:07.013
You are a songwriter.
Now, go write songs."

222
00:14:07.096 --> 00:14:09.348
[playing "Ruin"]

223
00:14:16.522 --> 00:14:18.566
-Here we go!
-[audience cheering]

224
00:14:19.734 --> 00:14:25.156
♪ No, I'm not trying
To ruin your happiness, baby ♪

225
00:14:25.239 --> 00:14:29.702
♪ But, darling, don't you know
That I'm the only one, yeah ♪

226
00:14:30.912 --> 00:14:32.538
New York!

227
00:14:32.622 --> 00:14:35.917
["Can't Take My Eyes Off You"
playing on stereo]

228
00:14:42.298 --> 00:14:45.051
♪ You're just too good to be true ♪

229
00:14:46.594 --> 00:14:49.764
♪ Can't take my eyes off of you ♪

230
00:14:51.099 --> 00:14:52.809
You don't hear songs that say,

231
00:14:52.892 --> 00:14:56.104
"You're just too good to be true.
Can't take my eyes off of you."

232
00:14:56.187 --> 00:14:58.856
["Can't Take My Eyes Off You"
continues playing]

233
00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.776
Even, like, those trumpets going...
[imitating trumpets]

234
00:15:01.859 --> 00:15:04.362
Like, all that trumpet stuff
is really cool, right?

235
00:15:05.404 --> 00:15:07.490
Feels, like, so, like, grandiose.

236
00:15:08.241 --> 00:15:12.078
There's something about that I think about
when it comes to the next album.

237
00:15:13.121 --> 00:15:15.331
Something about, like, that, like...

238
00:15:15.414 --> 00:15:19.710
feeling, that, like,
all-around, like, overdose of love.

239
00:15:20.878 --> 00:15:22.046
[guitar strumming]

240
00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:23.881
♪ Here I sleep in London ♪

241
00:15:23.965 --> 00:15:26.801
♪ 'Cause I could spend
A hundred days in-- ♪

242
00:15:26.884 --> 00:15:30.388
Could you go, "Counting back from 100,
so I can fall asleep faster"?

243
00:15:30.471 --> 00:15:32.849
♪ Sleep in London
I count back from 100 ♪

244
00:15:32.932 --> 00:15:33.891
-That's cool.
-Yeah.

245
00:15:34.475 --> 00:15:35.726
I was feeling like a...

246
00:15:36.519 --> 00:15:38.646
[Scott] Love the echo
after "Hello, hello."

247
00:15:38.729 --> 00:15:41.774
♪ Hello, hello, hello
Can I get an echo? ♪

248
00:15:41.858 --> 00:15:43.359
♪ Purple, red, and yellow ♪

249
00:15:43.442 --> 00:15:46.863
[vocalizing]

250
00:15:46.946 --> 00:15:49.073
[Scott] ♪ Head down on the pillow ♪

251
00:15:49.157 --> 00:15:51.075
♪ Something that I... ♪

252
00:15:53.953 --> 00:15:56.539
♪ When I'm not with you ♪

253
00:15:57.123 --> 00:15:59.959
♪ I just close my eyes ♪

254
00:16:01.586 --> 00:16:02.545
"All I have to do."

255
00:16:02.628 --> 00:16:06.257
♪ All I have to do ♪

256
00:16:07.592 --> 00:16:11.179
[both] ♪ Is dream, dream, dream, dream ♪

257
00:16:11.262 --> 00:16:12.096
[man] Yeah.

258
00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:16.809
[all] ♪ About you, about you, about you ♪

259
00:16:16.893 --> 00:16:18.436
That's the one.

260
00:16:18.519 --> 00:16:21.314
[all] ♪ About you, about you, about you ♪

261
00:16:21.397 --> 00:16:23.357
[recorded music-only track playing]

262
00:16:23.441 --> 00:16:24.775
It sounds better without.

263
00:16:25.568 --> 00:16:27.820
-[man 1] Without?
-[man 2] Sounds better.

264
00:16:35.453 --> 00:16:38.623
♪ Hello, hello, hello
Can I hear an echo? ♪

265
00:16:38.706 --> 00:16:42.293
♪ Purple, red, and yellow
I can't wait to get home ♪

266
00:16:42.376 --> 00:16:46.923
♪ Head down on the pillow
Holding you is all I think about ♪

267
00:16:47.673 --> 00:16:48.758
♪ Yeah ♪

268
00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:51.552
♪ When I'm a...
When I'm... ♪

269
00:16:51.636 --> 00:16:52.720
Again.

270
00:16:52.803 --> 00:16:54.805
♪ When I'm a... ♪

271
00:16:57.475 --> 00:17:00.519
♪ When I'm apart from you ♪

272
00:17:01.103 --> 00:17:04.357
♪ I just close my eyes ♪

273
00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:08.611
♪ All I have to do ♪

274
00:17:09.779 --> 00:17:11.906
Okay, George, punch me on "Close my eyes".

275
00:17:11.989 --> 00:17:16.744
♪ Close my eyes
Close my eyes, close my eyes ♪

276
00:17:20.373 --> 00:17:21.249
It's pretty cool,

277
00:17:21.332 --> 00:17:24.460
she rents an apartment in West Village,
so we're staying there,

278
00:17:24.543 --> 00:17:27.046
We wake up in the morning,
like, "This is fucked."

279
00:17:27.129 --> 00:17:30.174
And we have to wake up
and both separately get in SUVs

280
00:17:30.258 --> 00:17:31.634
to head to the same place.

281
00:17:31.717 --> 00:17:33.344
-[man] Yeah.
-It's pretty cool.

282
00:17:36.055 --> 00:17:39.267
I'm like, "I gotta leave at 8:30."
She's like, "Me too." 

283
00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:41.727
It's almost like living
a taste of a normal life

284
00:17:41.811 --> 00:17:44.397
in the least normal-life way.

285
00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:48.109
Getting all my clothes on
and running to the café for an Americano.

286
00:17:48.192 --> 00:17:51.737
Then you guys pulled up, and I was like,
"Right, we're going to work."

287
00:17:55.324 --> 00:17:57.326
-[man] How you doing?
-Good, how are you?

288
00:18:00.162 --> 00:18:01.872
[drums tuning]

289
00:18:01.956 --> 00:18:07.169
♪ I can't write one song 
That's not about you, baby ♪

290
00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:13.342
♪ Is it too late to tell you that ♪

291
00:18:13.426 --> 00:18:16.929
♪ Everything means nothing 
If I can't have you? ♪

292
00:18:17.013 --> 00:18:17.930
♪ No ♪

293
00:18:35.364 --> 00:18:37.825
♪ Every touch is ooh-la-la-la ♪

294
00:18:37.908 --> 00:18:38.743
We go this way.

295
00:18:38.826 --> 00:18:41.537
So, when I step this way,
what do I do with my arm?

296
00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:45.291
Boom. So this hand, when you step over...
You step over here, boom.

297
00:18:45.374 --> 00:18:46.792
-You look back...
-Love that.

298
00:18:46.876 --> 00:18:48.878
...and then you come around...

299
00:18:49.879 --> 00:18:51.005
-So--
-Okay, got it.

300
00:18:51.088 --> 00:18:53.007
-You're going to the other side.
-No.

301
00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:55.134
-All your weight is here.
-Yep.

302
00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:59.430
And then, you know
about the outside edge...

303
00:18:59.513 --> 00:19:00.639
This side?

304
00:19:01.849 --> 00:19:03.517
[woman] Yeah, making sure that...

305
00:19:03.601 --> 00:19:05.603
[strumming chords]

306
00:19:06.937 --> 00:19:10.024
[slow, pensive music]

307
00:19:25.748 --> 00:19:30.127
[Cabello] ♪ I love it 
When you call me señorita ♪

308
00:19:30.211 --> 00:19:35.091
♪ I wish I could pretend
I didn't need ya ♪

309
00:19:48.896 --> 00:19:50.648
[inaudible]

310
00:19:50.731 --> 00:19:52.858
Okay. Super cozy.

311
00:19:52.942 --> 00:19:54.318
-Super cozy.
-Yeah.

312
00:19:55.069 --> 00:19:57.571
[kisses] I love you.

313
00:19:58.572 --> 00:20:00.157
-Do you know that?
-I know.

314
00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:02.576
[kisses]

315
00:20:03.786 --> 00:20:07.790
[man 1] Thank you, everyone, good to go.
Places. Let's start rehearsal, please.

316
00:20:16.716 --> 00:20:19.343
[man 2] We're ready to roll
when you folks are ready.

317
00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:25.057
[Shawn] Camila, she was in Fifth Harmony,
and we were both opening.

318
00:20:25.641 --> 00:20:27.476
[chuckles] My very first tour ever.

319
00:20:28.394 --> 00:20:30.438
And she was the act after me.

320
00:20:30.938 --> 00:20:32.273
I was first in the lineup,

321
00:20:32.356 --> 00:20:34.734
with the shortest set,
and then they went on.

322
00:20:35.359 --> 00:20:36.402
Five years ago, man.

323
00:20:40.156 --> 00:20:41.323
[Cabello] He was so...

324
00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:44.660
super hyper-focused
on what he was doing.

325
00:20:44.785 --> 00:20:46.370
I never saw him the whole tour.

326
00:20:46.954 --> 00:20:51.083
He was constantly in and out of his bus,
playing guitar, writing songs with Geoff.

327
00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.378
I thought he was cute, but I was like,

328
00:20:54.462 --> 00:20:57.256
"He's... He's doing other stuff, 
so whatever."

329
00:20:57.381 --> 00:20:58.466
[laughs]

330
00:20:59.842 --> 00:21:03.095
And then, I guess it must have been
about four or five years ago,

331
00:21:03.721 --> 00:21:05.890
we were backstage
at this Taylor Swift show.

332
00:21:07.141 --> 00:21:09.518
I went to his dressing room to say hi.

333
00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:13.814
And we, like, started writing this song.

334
00:21:15.649 --> 00:21:18.986
And then after that, we, like,
spent a lot of time with each other

335
00:21:19.069 --> 00:21:20.696
because we had the song together

336
00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:23.783
and we did
a whole Jingle Ball tour together.

337
00:21:23.866 --> 00:21:29.580
And that's really when
the fucking saga started.

338
00:21:32.666 --> 00:21:33.959
I really liked him.

339
00:21:35.794 --> 00:21:37.213
I guess he liked me, but...

340
00:21:39.423 --> 00:21:41.675
I don't really know. [laughs]

341
00:21:44.845 --> 00:21:46.472
[Shawn] For the past four years,

342
00:21:46.555 --> 00:21:49.266
just being friends
and not seeing each other very often

343
00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:51.435
to finally being able to be together,

344
00:21:51.519 --> 00:21:54.772
she was always there
to look out for me as a human being.

345
00:21:54.855 --> 00:21:58.067
She's got my back, and I think
that's what your partner's for.

346
00:21:59.151 --> 00:22:02.613
We're in New York, and my song
comes on the radio or something,

347
00:22:02.696 --> 00:22:04.865
and the fact comes up
that it's about her.

348
00:22:05.449 --> 00:22:08.452
And I'm like, "Yeah, it's about you.
Everything's about you.

349
00:22:08.536 --> 00:22:10.204
They've always been about you."

350
00:22:10.287 --> 00:22:13.499
She goes, "What do you mean?" 
I'm like, "They're all about you.

351
00:22:13.582 --> 00:22:15.376
Like, every song I ever wrote."

352
00:22:15.459 --> 00:22:19.046
And I'm rhyming off the songs like,
"Treat You Better," all these songs.

353
00:22:19.129 --> 00:22:22.550
She's like, "Oh, my God."
She literally had no idea.

354
00:22:22.633 --> 00:22:25.177
This whole time,
I thought she, like, knew.

355
00:22:27.346 --> 00:22:31.058
I don't think I'll be able
to write songs that really do it justice,

356
00:22:31.141 --> 00:22:34.228
that can really capture
the things and the feelings with her.

357
00:22:35.646 --> 00:22:38.440
I think it's like
when you see a moon or stars

358
00:22:38.524 --> 00:22:41.026
and you try to take
a photo of it with your iPhone,

359
00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:43.988
and then you just can't,
it just doesn't look good.

360
00:22:44.655 --> 00:22:47.908
And you're like, "It's not 
supposed to be captured." You know?

361
00:22:49.034 --> 00:22:50.703
It's just supposed to be for us.

362
00:22:55.249 --> 00:22:57.960
[Cabello] Want to do it again for fun,
stuff like that?

363
00:22:58.043 --> 00:22:59.545
Play around just to get loose.

364
00:22:59.628 --> 00:23:00.462
[vocalizing]

365
00:23:00.546 --> 00:23:04.258
[both] ♪ I love it 
When you call me señorita ♪

366
00:23:04.341 --> 00:23:08.387
♪ I wish I could pretend
I didn't need ya ♪

367
00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:11.473
♪ But every touch is ooh la la la ♪

368
00:23:11.557 --> 00:23:13.559
♪ It's true, la la la ♪

369
00:23:13.642 --> 00:23:15.686
♪ Ooh, I should be running ♪

370
00:23:15.769 --> 00:23:18.564
♪ Ooh, you keep me coming for ya ♪

371
00:23:18.647 --> 00:23:20.357
♪ Locked in the hotel ♪

372
00:23:20.441 --> 00:23:23.360
♪ There's just some things
That never change ♪

373
00:23:24.278 --> 00:23:27.448
♪ But friends don't know
The way you taste ♪

374
00:23:29.783 --> 00:23:34.121
♪ You know it's been a long time coming
Don't you let me fall, oh ♪

375
00:23:34.204 --> 00:23:36.206
[both]
♪ Ooh, when your lips undress me ♪

376
00:23:36.332 --> 00:23:37.875
♪ Hooked on your tongue ♪

377
00:23:37.958 --> 00:23:40.252
♪ Ooh, love, your kiss is deadly ♪

378
00:23:40.336 --> 00:23:42.004
♪ Don't stop ♪

379
00:23:42.087 --> 00:23:45.341
-[whispers] Boom. Boom, boom. Boom, boom.
-[exhales sharply]

380
00:23:45.424 --> 00:23:46.842
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

381
00:23:46.926 --> 00:23:48.802
-[both laugh]
-[sighs]

382
00:23:48.886 --> 00:23:51.347
Okay. Good. Let's sing another song.

383
00:23:51.430 --> 00:23:54.767
What's a song for fun?
Literally, any song, but ours.

384
00:23:56.268 --> 00:23:58.437
♪ It's not a silly little moment ♪

385
00:23:58.520 --> 00:23:59.855
Fuck, yeah.

386
00:23:59.938 --> 00:24:03.400
[both] ♪ It's not the storm 
Before the calm ♪

387
00:24:03.484 --> 00:24:05.986
♪ This is the deep and dying breath of ♪

388
00:24:06.946 --> 00:24:09.657
♪ That we've been working on ♪

389
00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:12.534
♪ We're going down ♪

390
00:24:13.869 --> 00:24:16.038
♪ And you know that we're doomed ♪

391
00:24:16.747 --> 00:24:23.045
♪ My dear, we're slow dancing 
In a burning room ♪

392
00:24:23.754 --> 00:24:30.052
♪ My dear, we're slow dancing 
In a burning room ♪

393
00:24:30.135 --> 00:24:33.472
[gentle piano music]

394
00:24:33.555 --> 00:24:34.848
[man] Step back.

395
00:24:34.932 --> 00:24:37.101
-[people clamoring]
-[man] Step back.

396
00:24:38.352 --> 00:24:40.354
[women screaming]

397
00:24:47.486 --> 00:24:50.072
Shawn! Shawn!

398
00:24:50.155 --> 00:24:52.199
[camera shutters clicking]

399
00:24:53.075 --> 00:24:55.035
[photographer] Shawn, all the way down.

400
00:24:55.119 --> 00:24:58.080
Shawn! Shawn, right here for me, man.
Shawn!

401
00:24:58.163 --> 00:24:59.581
Shawn, right here!

402
00:24:59.665 --> 00:25:01.041
[man] Mr. Mendes!

403
00:25:01.125 --> 00:25:02.918
Shawn, one more here.

404
00:25:03.002 --> 00:25:05.546
[people continue screaming excitedly]

405
00:25:10.175 --> 00:25:11.719
Oh, my God!

406
00:25:13.053 --> 00:25:15.806
[gentle music continues]

407
00:25:24.648 --> 00:25:27.651
[man] It's insane. That was insane!

408
00:25:28.235 --> 00:25:30.112
That was a really calm red carpet.

409
00:25:30.779 --> 00:25:32.948
[laughs] I'm serious.

410
00:25:33.032 --> 00:25:35.159
-[man] That was calm?
-That was calm, dude.

411
00:25:35.659 --> 00:25:38.495
[audience cheering loudly]

412
00:25:46.920 --> 00:25:49.298
[Cabello] Wait, my, uh... 
My shoe! My shoe!

413
00:25:50.174 --> 00:25:51.592
Oh, no!

414
00:25:52.468 --> 00:25:53.677
My shoe.

415
00:25:55.053 --> 00:25:59.308
[Shawn] Is there a proper way to do this?
I swear, I'm gonna tie a double knot.

416
00:26:00.684 --> 00:26:02.186
[woman] Who's ready?

417
00:26:02.269 --> 00:26:04.688
[vocalizing]

418
00:26:04.772 --> 00:26:07.232
♪ It meant something to ya ♪

419
00:26:07.316 --> 00:26:10.819
[Cabello] ♪ Ooh, you keep me 
Coming for ya ♪

420
00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:12.696
Can I have water?

421
00:26:13.781 --> 00:26:15.407
Come on, it's time, let's go.

422
00:26:15.491 --> 00:26:17.493
[inaudible]

423
00:26:19.787 --> 00:26:22.498
[audience cheering loudly]

424
00:26:33.592 --> 00:26:36.011
[Shawn] At this moment in time,
during the summer

425
00:26:36.094 --> 00:26:38.430
of whatever you want to name this summer,

426
00:26:38.514 --> 00:26:40.891
during "Señorita"
and "If I Can't Have You"...

427
00:26:43.352 --> 00:26:45.687
Camila and I are staying
in an apartment in NYC

428
00:26:45.771 --> 00:26:47.481
for the very first time alone.

429
00:26:48.690 --> 00:26:51.985
And making eggs and trying
to figure out how to use a Keurig.

430
00:26:52.569 --> 00:26:53.862
Normal things, you know?

431
00:26:54.905 --> 00:26:57.825
This is really cool,
to just be, like, a 21-year-old guy.

432
00:26:58.408 --> 00:26:59.451
And getting older...

433
00:27:00.327 --> 00:27:02.246
That's happening for me too.

434
00:27:02.329 --> 00:27:04.164
[Cabello laughs]

435
00:27:04.248 --> 00:27:06.124
[man] Give it up for Shawn Mendes!

436
00:27:06.208 --> 00:27:08.210
[audience cheering loudly]

437
00:27:15.467 --> 00:27:18.512
[slow, pensive music]

438
00:27:28.230 --> 00:27:30.274
Camila Cabello, everybody!

439
00:27:30.357 --> 00:27:32.359
[audience cheering]

440
00:27:40.242 --> 00:27:41.285
[Shawn] I'm nervous.

441
00:27:42.119 --> 00:27:44.413
Yeah, I feel anxious to go home right now.

442
00:27:45.289 --> 00:27:46.707
[man] How long has it been?

443
00:27:47.207 --> 00:27:48.458
Three and half months.

444
00:27:49.459 --> 00:27:50.377
It's a long time.

445
00:27:51.837 --> 00:27:55.299
I'm excited to have a couple days off
and be with friends and family.

446
00:27:55.382 --> 00:27:57.217
Yeah. So excited.

447
00:28:00.220 --> 00:28:02.472
I'm so lucky to have a friend like Brian.

448
00:28:03.307 --> 00:28:04.975
He loves them anyway.

449
00:28:05.517 --> 00:28:08.645
He works hard
at keeping me in the real world.

450
00:28:08.729 --> 00:28:11.315
If we had our own FIFA cards, 
you'd probably have--

451
00:28:11.398 --> 00:28:14.109
-I'd have a high rating.
-You'd probably be 76 passing,

452
00:28:14.193 --> 00:28:15.485
-I'd be 82.
-Not a chance.

453
00:28:15.569 --> 00:28:19.072
-I'd be rated a 93, you'd be rated an 87.
-[snorts, laughs]

454
00:28:19.156 --> 00:28:20.157
What's Ronaldo?

455
00:28:20.699 --> 00:28:23.160
Ronaldo? I think Ronaldo's a 94.

456
00:28:23.243 --> 00:28:25.871
-Yeah, I'm a 93.
-[both laugh]

457
00:28:25.954 --> 00:28:30.125
Without him, I don't know,
I'd probably be, like, pretty crazy.

458
00:28:30.208 --> 00:28:32.294
Can you match my tone?
That's my question.

459
00:28:32.377 --> 00:28:33.837
[flatly] ♪ Yeah ♪

460
00:28:33.921 --> 00:28:35.047
♪ Yeah ♪

461
00:28:35.130 --> 00:28:37.132
[laughs]

462
00:28:37.216 --> 00:28:39.259
♪ Yeah ♪

463
00:28:39.343 --> 00:28:42.054
[Shawn] He just connects me
with friends from home.

464
00:28:45.432 --> 00:28:48.393
I'm probably closer with my friends
from home now than ever.

465
00:28:48.477 --> 00:28:50.479
-Oh!
-They were all supporting me

466
00:28:50.562 --> 00:28:53.315
from the first time
"Life of the Party" came out,

467
00:28:53.398 --> 00:28:54.983
and now we're here together.

468
00:28:57.277 --> 00:28:59.738
I want them to look around
and be proud of it

469
00:29:00.405 --> 00:29:03.742
and be like,
"This is just as much ours as it is his."

470
00:29:07.496 --> 00:29:08.747
"Look, guys, we made it.

471
00:29:10.457 --> 00:29:11.625
How beautiful is this?"

472
00:29:14.711 --> 00:29:16.964
All right, bedroom.
You did me great. Thanks.

473
00:29:17.547 --> 00:29:18.924
I'll see you next time.

474
00:29:19.508 --> 00:29:20.842
Thank God I'm leaving you.

475
00:29:21.593 --> 00:29:23.011
Double guitar.

476
00:29:23.095 --> 00:29:24.304
Let's go, bro.

477
00:29:35.816 --> 00:29:36.984
Good to see you, man.

478
00:29:37.067 --> 00:29:39.194
-Good to see you, welcome back.
-Thank you.

479
00:29:39.277 --> 00:29:41.488
You rock! You rock! You rock!

480
00:29:43.282 --> 00:29:46.118
[delicate music playing]

481
00:29:46.868 --> 00:29:47.703
Welcome.

482
00:29:47.786 --> 00:29:50.497
-It's been unlocked for three months.
-[Brian laughs]

483
00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:51.456
Let's go.

484
00:29:51.540 --> 00:29:54.459
Welcome to my cozy house!
It smells great in here.

485
00:30:01.842 --> 00:30:03.552
Okay, everything seems right.

486
00:30:04.303 --> 00:30:06.138
How's your room, Brian? Seems right?

487
00:30:06.805 --> 00:30:07.848
[Brian] Checks out.

488
00:30:12.602 --> 00:30:14.271
[Shawn] Everything checks out?

489
00:30:14.354 --> 00:30:15.814
[Brian] Oh, yeah.

490
