-♪ Ooh ♪

817
00:49:08.946 --> 00:49:09.864
You are?

818
00:49:09.947 --> 00:49:11.615
-Yeah.
-You're just quiet in here.

819
00:49:11.699 --> 00:49:12.533
♪ Ooh... ♪

820
00:49:12.616 --> 00:49:15.077
Where are you?
We'll just turn you up a little.

821
00:49:15.161 --> 00:49:16.328
♪ Teach me how to ♪

822
00:49:16.412 --> 00:49:17.705
Yeah, we need that.

823
00:49:17.788 --> 00:49:20.332
[song playing]

824
00:49:22.835 --> 00:49:26.046
♪ Teach me, teach me, teach me
How to love ♪

825
00:49:26.797 --> 00:49:28.340
[plucking melody]

826
00:49:28.424 --> 00:49:31.844
[Shawn] I've definitely always felt
the pressure to make music that's

827
00:49:31.927 --> 00:49:34.096
better than what I've done before.

828
00:49:36.974 --> 00:49:39.643
I feel this time around,
I'm in the studio...

829
00:49:40.644 --> 00:49:43.772
kind of just being like,
"Okay, whatever comes, comes."

830
00:49:44.481 --> 00:49:47.359
[playing with melodies and chords]

831
00:49:54.617 --> 00:49:56.035
We recording, George?

832
00:49:58.746 --> 00:50:02.416
[Shawn] You have to not only accept
imperfection but embrace imperfection,

833
00:50:02.499 --> 00:50:07.880
because that imperfection in that moment
is what turns into magic in the next.

834
00:50:09.089 --> 00:50:12.968
♪ Look up at the stars ♪

835
00:50:13.052 --> 00:50:15.763
♪ They're like pieces of art ♪

836
00:50:16.847 --> 00:50:20.100
♪ Floating above the planet ♪

837
00:50:21.310 --> 00:50:25.189
♪ You know we've come so far ♪

838
00:50:25.272 --> 00:50:28.651
♪ The universe is ours ♪

839
00:50:29.318 --> 00:50:32.696
♪ And I'm not gonna let you down ♪

840
00:50:35.783 --> 00:50:38.535
♪ It's a Friday night and streetlights ♪

841
