I'm so sorry, guys. My voice is
cutting out on me so much tonight.

870
00:52:28.479 --> 00:52:30.356
I'll need your help as much as I can.

871
00:52:30.439 --> 00:52:34.318
I promise to sing my heart out,
but I only got what I got in my voice,

872
00:52:34.401 --> 00:52:36.236
so thank you so much.

873
00:52:43.827 --> 00:52:45.120
They're looping.

874
00:52:45.204 --> 00:52:46.872
You tell me when you want to go.

875
00:52:51.752 --> 00:52:54.296
Fucking hell, man. I just...

876
00:52:55.214 --> 00:52:57.925
-What you just did just then...
-No, man, I...

877
00:52:58.008 --> 00:52:59.301
It's insane.

878
00:53:03.722 --> 00:53:05.808
[inaudible]

879
00:53:08.227 --> 00:53:10.562
[pensive music]

880
00:53:11.689 --> 00:53:13.899
[Shawn] We're on a 104-show tour, and...

881
00:53:14.983 --> 00:53:16.485
half of me right now is like,

882
00:53:16.568 --> 00:53:19.029
"Make sure you say you're grateful,"
because I am.

883
00:53:19.113 --> 00:53:21.156
In the biggest way, I'm so grateful.

884
00:53:21.240 --> 00:53:24.993
I love these performances.
I've never had more fun in my life, but...

885
00:53:25.077 --> 00:53:26.829
[Shawn and Karen talk indistinctly]

886
00:53:26.912 --> 00:53:29.790
I also want to hang with my parents, 
watch movies.

887
00:53:29.873 --> 00:53:31.625
You're gonna do a tree at my house?

888
00:53:31.709 --> 00:53:33.919
Yeah. I'll do your tree, but nothing else.

889
00:53:34.753 --> 00:53:35.629
-Yeah.
-...school.

890
00:53:35.713 --> 00:53:38.549
[Shawn] Drive around a suburb,
lay on a soccer field...

891
00:53:39.133 --> 00:53:41.802
smoke a joint
and stare at the stars with my friends

892
00:53:41.885 --> 00:53:44.430
and, like, eat some beef jerky.
[laughs]

893
00:53:44.513 --> 00:53:48.600
And, like, really, like,
small-town thoughts.

894
00:53:48.684 --> 00:53:50.602
You know, those things are like...

895
00:53:50.686 --> 00:53:52.938
I think I miss that 
a little bit right now.

896
00:53:53.021 --> 00:53:54.731
It's pretty intense all the time.

897
00:54:00.070 --> 00:54:01.697
I really think about that a lot.

898
00:54:04.533 --> 00:54:07.286
If I tell the world
that I'm just a normal human,

899
00:54:07.369 --> 00:54:09.538
are they going to stop
coming to the shows

900
00:54:09.621 --> 00:54:12.082
and listening to the music, and, like,

901
00:54:12.166 --> 00:54:14.460
is all the craziness going to stop?

902
00:54:14.543 --> 00:54:16.962
Then you're like,
"Maybe I shouldn't tell them.

903
00:54:17.045 --> 00:54:18.422
I should keep the trick up.

904
00:54:18.505 --> 00:54:21.800
Maybe I should pretend that
I'm Superman for a little bit longer."

905
00:54:23.510 --> 00:54:27.431
[gentle piano music]

906
00:54:29.057 --> 00:54:30.058
Just played.

907
00:54:30.726 --> 00:54:32.644
Writing a little message on Instagram.

908
00:54:33.353 --> 00:54:35.105
"Feeling overwhelmed by life today.

909
00:54:35.189 --> 00:54:37.858
I'm right here right now, 
and it's beautiful.

910
00:54:39.735 --> 00:54:41.111
And it's so beautiful.

911
00:54:43.822 --> 00:54:45.449
And it's so beautiful."

912
00:54:53.582 --> 00:54:54.958
That's all I got for you.

913
00:54:57.336 --> 00:55:00.631
[distant Latin music playing]

914
00:55:07.054 --> 00:55:09.056
[Shawn playing melody on guitar]

915
00:55:15.646 --> 00:55:19.149
I've been trying to figure it out
since it started, you know,

916
00:55:19.233 --> 00:55:21.610
and I have a billion different ways...

917
00:55:21.693 --> 00:55:25.864
People'll be like, "Why'd this happen 
to you?" I have a lot of logical answers,

918
00:55:25.948 --> 00:55:28.742
but none of them are satisfying, you know?

919
00:55:30.953 --> 00:55:34.623
-[Eric Vetro performing voice exercise]
-[Shawn repeating after him]

920
00:55:37.668 --> 00:55:40.838
[voice exercising continues]

921
00:55:40.921 --> 00:55:42.256
I'm constantly warming up,

922
00:55:42.339 --> 00:55:45.717
and I'm constantly checking my voice
out of fear of the fact that...

923
00:55:46.301 --> 00:55:49.680
one day I'm going to go to sing
and it's going to just not come out.

924
00:55:49.763 --> 00:55:52.641
[Vetro] Open the back of your throat,
take a deep breath.

925
00:55:52.724 --> 00:55:55.310
[Shawn performing vocal exercise]

926
00:55:58.272 --> 00:56:00.232
[Vetro] Really loose and open.

927
00:56:00.315 --> 00:56:03.360
[Shawn singing scale]

928
00:56:04.528 --> 00:56:07.531
[vocalizing]

929
00:56:14.121 --> 00:56:18.000
[voice rising to a high pitch]
♪ Yeah ♪

930
00:56:18.083 --> 00:56:20.085
[playing "Youth"]

931
00:56:26.925 --> 00:56:29.219
[all] ♪ You can't take my youth away ♪

932
00:56:29.303 --> 00:56:31.430
♪ This soul of mine will never break ♪

933
00:56:31.513 --> 00:56:33.890
[audience]
♪ As long as I wake up today ♪

934
00:56:33.974 --> 00:56:35.601
♪ You can't take my youth away ♪

935
00:56:39.313 --> 00:56:40.731
[Shawn] What are they doing?

936
00:56:40.814 --> 00:56:43.775
[man] They're running 'cause they see
other people running.

937
00:56:43.859 --> 00:56:45.694
Dude, the show's gonna be nuts.

938
00:56:46.945 --> 00:56:48.363
They're screaming.

939
00:56:48.447 --> 00:56:50.198
I wonder if the band's out there.

940
00:56:52.409 --> 00:56:55.537
Maybe it's 'cause I just posted
the Instagram of the sunset.

941
00:56:56.663 --> 00:56:58.373
Doesn't mean that I'm down there.

942
00:57:01.126 --> 00:57:03.128
[indistinct conversations]

943
00:57:11.178 --> 00:57:13.722
-Hi.
-This experience has been so good.

944
00:57:13.805 --> 00:57:15.807
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

945
00:57:15.891 --> 00:57:17.809
-I can't speak.
-It's okay.

946
00:57:17.893 --> 00:57:19.394
It's so nice to meet you.

947
00:57:19.478 --> 00:57:20.812
[indistinct]

948
00:57:20.896 --> 00:57:21.897
Yeah.

949
00:57:21.980 --> 00:57:23.982
[indistinct chatter]

950
00:57:25.609 --> 00:57:30.322
You make me feel connected to you
and connected to people around me,

951
00:57:30.405 --> 00:57:33.158
and I'm just so thankful, and I...

952
00:57:33.241 --> 00:57:34.868
-Oh, my God.
-[laughs]

953
00:57:34.952 --> 00:57:36.286
Should we take a photo?

954
00:57:41.917 --> 00:57:43.919
[laughing joyfully]

955
00:57:46.463 --> 00:57:49.675
[slow, gentle music]

956
00:57:57.557 --> 00:57:58.934
[women screaming]

957
00:58:00.352 --> 00:58:04.106
[Shawn] When you're pulling up to a hotel
in a country you've never been to,

958
00:58:04.189 --> 00:58:06.692
and there's 1,000 people
outside waiting for you...

959
00:58:10.445 --> 00:58:13.490
no matter how many times
you go through that, it feels...

960
00:58:14.700 --> 00:58:15.659
like a dream.

961
00:58:17.035 --> 00:58:19.454
I don't know
if that's ever going to feel normal.

962
00:58:20.706 --> 00:58:23.041
I don't know
if that's supposed to feel normal.

963
00:58:23.125 --> 00:58:25.836
[woman sobbing and talking indistinctly]

964
00:58:30.757 --> 00:58:33.218
I love you so much, thank you!

965
00:58:35.804 --> 00:58:37.639
Thank you so much!

966
00:58:38.390 --> 00:58:40.392
Thank you, Shawn! I love you!

967
00:58:42.644 --> 00:58:44.354
I love you so much.

968
00:58:44.438 --> 00:58:45.647
