969
00:58:54.531 --> 00:58:55.907
What's up, guys?

970
00:58:55.991 --> 00:59:00.412
We're, uh... We're in Brazil
on the last leg of the tour.

971
00:59:01.163 --> 00:59:02.914
I woke up feeling...

972
00:59:03.457 --> 00:59:05.417
[clears throat] ...pretty sick today.

973
00:59:06.001 --> 00:59:09.212
The day before I'm gonna play
two stadiums in São Paulo.

974
00:59:09.296 --> 00:59:11.423
But you know what? It's okay because...

975
00:59:12.048 --> 00:59:15.010
I watched some Kobe Bryant YouTube videos
and I feel great.

976
00:59:15.093 --> 00:59:16.052
[clears throat]

977
00:59:16.136 --> 00:59:18.597
[playing upbeat song on guitar]

978
00:59:29.024 --> 00:59:32.152
-'Cause I had swelling on my right cord.
-Yeah, that's swollen.

979
00:59:32.235 --> 00:59:35.489
Just wanna check.
I have volume if I wanna bring it back.

980
00:59:35.572 --> 00:59:38.450
-Okay, you'll just--
-But I just am choosing not to. Yeah.

981
00:59:39.367 --> 00:59:40.452
Yeah.

982
00:59:40.535 --> 00:59:42.329
[inaudible]

983
00:59:42.954 --> 00:59:44.956
[vocalizing]

984
00:59:52.798 --> 00:59:54.800
[doctor speaking indistinctly]

985
00:59:57.427 --> 00:59:58.678
Thank you so much.

986
01:00:07.354 --> 01:00:10.357
[slow, reflecting music]

987
01:00:17.113 --> 01:00:22.661
[vocalizing]

988
01:00:26.748 --> 01:00:28.250
[Vetro] Hey, how's it going?

989
01:00:28.333 --> 01:00:30.335
It's going. It's going.

990
01:00:30.418 --> 01:00:32.128
Just listen to this. This is...

991
01:00:33.672 --> 01:00:35.799
[vocalizing]

992
01:00:42.264 --> 01:00:45.475
I don't know. It makes me very nervous.

993
01:00:46.643 --> 01:00:48.645
What time is it there right now?

994
01:00:49.271 --> 01:00:50.230
It's 3:30.

995
01:00:51.565 --> 01:00:53.525
And what time is the show?

996
01:00:53.608 --> 01:00:54.693
8:30.

997
01:00:56.278 --> 01:00:59.364
[vocalizing]

998
01:01:03.201 --> 01:01:05.829
I don't think it's a good idea.
That's my feeling.

999
01:01:06.413 --> 01:01:07.998
I want to bring you to Cez,

1000
01:01:08.081 --> 01:01:12.460
just so you can say to him,
based off of...

1001
01:01:12.961 --> 01:01:15.380
You're saying,
based off of how my voice sounds--

1002
01:01:15.463 --> 01:01:18.133
Based off of that,
you shouldn't even be talking.

1003
01:01:18.216 --> 01:01:20.802
I'm nervous that you'll hurt yourself,
and then...

1004
01:01:23.305 --> 01:01:24.222
Can you hear me?

1005
01:01:24.806 --> 01:01:25.640
Yeah.

1006
01:01:29.936 --> 01:01:30.770
Hey.

1007
01:01:33.690 --> 01:01:38.320
Yeah, so we FaceTimed Nasseri in
while we were in with the other doc.

1008
01:01:38.403 --> 01:01:41.364
So he was there
looking at all the videos, all the scopes.

1009
01:01:41.448 --> 01:01:43.658
Everything was, like, through him.

1010
01:01:47.245 --> 01:01:51.333
Yeah, I completely trust
what you're saying, and agree.

1011
01:01:52.918 --> 01:01:54.461
The truth is in the singing.

1012
01:01:54.544 --> 01:01:56.463
Yeah,  a hundred percent.
[chuckles]

1013
01:01:56.546 --> 01:01:58.548
It's there or it's not. Yeah, totally.

1014
01:02:01.259 --> 01:02:04.471
Okay, if you're saying
it's detrimental to warm up right now,

1015
01:02:04.554 --> 01:02:06.222
then let's not do that.

1016
01:02:07.224 --> 01:02:09.017
All good. Thanks, Eric.

1017
01:02:09.809 --> 01:02:11.102
All right. Bye, dude.

1018
01:02:12.020 --> 01:02:16.191
Just so you know, I've made it very aware
that we have 11 more shows after this.

1019
01:02:16.274 --> 01:02:19.778
If we're in any way pushing through
this show to get this show done,

1020
01:02:19.861 --> 01:02:21.696
it'll be to the detriment of those.

1021
01:02:21.780 --> 01:02:25.367
-We'll have to start thinking about--
-The show scenario. Yeah.

1022
01:02:27.619 --> 01:02:29.329
Dr. Nasseri, it's Cez here.

1023
01:02:29.412 --> 01:02:31.331
I'm going to merge a call with Eric,

1024
01:02:31.414 --> 01:02:33.375
and you've got me and Shawn here.

1025
01:02:34.167 --> 01:02:36.628
[Vetro] So, Shawn, any improvement yet?

1026
01:02:36.711 --> 01:02:37.587
No.

1027
01:02:38.713 --> 01:02:43.093
-Five hours to show time, Cez?
-Yeah, we're 30 minutes to doors.

1028
01:02:45.136 --> 01:02:48.974
-Thirty minutes to doors? Why so early?
-'Cause it's a stadium.

1029
01:02:51.142 --> 01:02:51.977
Right.

1030
01:02:52.060 --> 01:02:55.480
[Nasseri] I was just gonna say,
we've seen people who have said,

1031
01:02:55.563 --> 01:02:57.774
"I'm just going to muscle through it",

1032
01:02:57.857 --> 01:03:01.778
and they completely hemorrhaged,
and then they needed surgery.

1033
01:03:01.861 --> 01:03:05.865
I mean, I know it's a really
overwhelming thing to cancel, but--

1034
01:03:05.949 --> 01:03:08.285
[Vetro] I'm gonna step in now and tell you

1035
01:03:08.368 --> 01:03:11.913
you have really no voice,
we have 11 shows to go.

1036
01:03:12.664 --> 01:03:14.124
For an outside stadium,

1037
01:03:14.207 --> 01:03:17.168
you're gonna hurt yourself
for the next 11.

1038
01:03:18.086 --> 01:03:20.338
-Yeah.
-[Vetro] What do you think, Shawn?

1039
01:03:22.632 --> 01:03:25.760
I don't know. I'm not in a good place
to make any decisions.

1040
01:03:25.844 --> 01:03:27.387
[Darke] He's overwhelmed.

1041
01:03:27.929 --> 01:03:31.474
And just to be clear, 
both of you are saying

1042
01:03:31.558 --> 01:03:33.351
we should cancel the show, right?

1043
01:03:34.811 --> 01:03:37.314
-[Vetro] We're unanimous on that.
-[Darke] Okay.

1044
01:03:37.731 --> 01:03:40.400
Well, we'll get into it this side, 
and, um...

1045
01:03:40.942 --> 01:03:43.361
Yeah, we'll let you know
on the final decision,

1046
01:03:43.445 --> 01:03:44.946
and then we'll update you.

1047
01:03:46.031 --> 01:03:48.199
-[Vetro] Okay.
-All right. Thanks, dudes.

1048
01:03:49.451 --> 01:03:50.327
Take care.

1049
01:03:50.952 --> 01:03:53.246
[slow, reflective music]

1050
01:03:55.123 --> 01:03:56.666
See you in a bit, all right?

1051
01:04:02.922 --> 01:04:04.924
[sighs]

1052
01:04:07.802 --> 01:04:10.764
[breathes deeply]

1053
01:04:12.891 --> 01:04:14.392
[sniffles]

1054
01:04:14.476 --> 01:04:16.644
[crying softly]

1055
01:04:18.521 --> 01:04:19.647
[sniffles]

1056
01:04:30.617 --> 01:04:32.619
[indistinct clamoring]

1057
01:04:34.412 --> 01:04:36.623
[in Portuguese] Canceled!

1058
01:04:37.207 --> 01:04:38.792
"It breaks my heart to do this,

1059
01:04:38.875 --> 01:04:41.336
but my doctors told me
I cannot perform tonight,

1060
01:04:41.419 --> 01:04:43.880
or it would risk
long-term damage to my voice.

1061
01:04:43.963 --> 01:04:46.925
I love you all, and I apologize
from the bottom of my heart.

1062
01:04:47.008 --> 01:04:49.094
I wish I could be there on stage tonight.

1063
01:04:49.177 --> 01:04:51.679
I'll make it up to you
the next time I'm there."

1064
01:04:59.979 --> 01:05:01.773
[breathes deeply]

1065
01:05:01.856 --> 01:05:03.149
[sniffles]

1066
01:05:06.319 --> 01:05:08.321
[water running]

1067
01:05:18.665 --> 01:05:21.918
[pensive music]

1068
01:05:49.654 --> 01:05:51.656
[phone ringing]

1069
01:05:53.950 --> 01:05:56.703
-[sighs, sniffles]
-[Karen] Aw, babe, I'm sorry.

1070
01:05:59.956 --> 01:06:01.624
It was a great show last night.

1071
01:06:01.708 --> 01:06:04.169
They got to see you there, babe.
It wasn't like...

1072
01:06:05.044 --> 01:06:07.380
you haven't been there.
They've seen you.

1073
01:06:07.463 --> 01:06:08.882
They've experienced it.

1074
01:06:08.965 --> 01:06:10.967
It wasn't like
you've never been there.

1075
01:06:11.718 --> 01:06:14.220
You told me you were sick.
You had a bad voice,

1076
01:06:14.304 --> 01:06:16.431
but you never told me
it was that serious.

1077
01:06:19.100 --> 01:06:20.935
[gentle piano music]

1078
01:06:21.019 --> 01:06:24.230
It's fine. You're fine.
It's not the end of the world, babe.

1079
01:06:25.982 --> 01:06:27.066
Take a breath.

1080
01:06:27.650 --> 01:06:28.651
[whispering] Yeah.

1081
01:06:28.735 --> 01:06:30.069
You can't help it.

1082
01:06:30.987 --> 01:06:32.947
[breathes deeply]

1083
01:06:33.031 --> 01:06:33.990
Love you.

1084
01:06:34.073 --> 01:06:36.159
You too, babe. I love you more.

1085
01:06:39.579 --> 01:06:41.456
You're good. You've got it.

1086
01:06:42.540 --> 01:06:44.000
You've got this, babe.

1087
01:06:46.503 --> 01:06:48.755
You know what,
the fans are gonna understand.

1088
01:06:51.090 --> 01:06:54.886
Yeah, said you were on vocal rest.
I didn't realize it was that serious.

1089
01:06:56.888 --> 01:06:59.224
[inaudible]

1090
01:07:02.810 --> 01:07:05.480
[gentle piano music continues]

1091
01:07:05.563 --> 01:07:07.565
[mouthing] Both of us.

1092
01:07:14.906 --> 01:07:16.908
[imperceptible]

1093
01:07:32.757 --> 01:07:36.010
[Shawn] It's so hard in that moment
to be like, "What can you do?"

1094
01:07:36.094 --> 01:07:39.055
because there's 40,000 people outside.

1095
01:07:40.265 --> 01:07:41.849
And you just feel...

1096
01:07:43.184 --> 01:07:45.561
the deepest pit in your stomach.

1097
01:08:00.910 --> 01:08:01.744
[sniffles]

1098
01:08:10.878 --> 01:08:12.880
Wow, it changes the mood real fast.

1099
01:08:15.091 --> 01:08:16.926
[Shawn] When we got to the hotel

1100
01:08:17.010 --> 01:08:19.971
and I was up in my room,
I was so upset with the situation,

1101
01:08:20.555 --> 01:08:23.182
and then I heard chanting from outside.

1102
01:08:23.266 --> 01:08:25.852
[people cheering, 
chanting in Portuguese]

1103
01:08:25.935 --> 01:08:28.730
[uplifting piano music]

1104
01:08:28.813 --> 01:08:29.981
I opened up my window,

1105
01:08:30.064 --> 01:08:32.859
and there was
2,000 people in the streets chanting.

1106
01:08:32.942 --> 01:08:35.361
[chanting in Portuguese]

1107
01:08:38.531 --> 01:08:41.034
And that is, like, beautiful.

1108
01:08:41.117 --> 01:08:43.119
[chanting continues]

1109
01:08:47.957 --> 01:08:49.959
Right then, I was like, "I can't even...

1110
01:08:51.961 --> 01:08:54.213
I can't even believe
how good people are." 

1111
01:08:54.297 --> 01:08:56.049
Just a really beautiful thing.

1112
01:08:57.008 --> 01:08:59.010
[shower running]

1113
01:09:07.477 --> 01:09:08.853
[typing on phone]

1114
01:09:10.521 --> 01:09:12.982
[automated female voice]
I was upset for a while.

1115
01:09:13.066 --> 01:09:14.484
[continues typing]

1116
01:09:14.567 --> 01:09:16.986
[acoustic guitar music]

1117
01:09:17.070 --> 01:09:21.741
I sat there in the stadium knowing
I was the reason it was all falling apart.

1118
01:09:22.408 --> 01:09:24.410
[continues typing]

1119
01:09:26.204 --> 01:09:29.332
The hardest part is
feeling like I let them down.

1120
01:09:32.251 --> 01:09:33.961
[continues typing]

1121
01:09:34.837 --> 01:09:39.509
These next 10 years are when
everything I do is going full speed.

1122
01:09:42.303 --> 01:09:44.764
It's like an athlete in their prime.

1123
01:09:44.847 --> 01:09:46.182
[strumming intensifies]

1124
01:09:48.059 --> 01:09:49.519
I have to keep going.

1125
01:10:38.317 --> 01:10:40.528
[Shawn] The heaviness of the tour

1126
01:10:40.611 --> 01:10:44.282
made me want to flip things around
and become more positive, you know?

1127
01:10:44.365 --> 01:10:47.910
And I'm writing about anxiety more as...

1128
01:10:50.121 --> 01:10:51.831
a companion I have to live with

1129
01:10:51.914 --> 01:10:54.250
and less of an enemy
that I'm trying to resist.

1130
01:10:54.333 --> 01:10:57.837
-[playing uplifting melody]
-[both singing indistinctly]

1131
01:11:10.349 --> 01:11:12.685
♪ Never thought 
It would get this far ♪

1132
01:11:12.769 --> 01:11:14.770
♪ Never thought it would get this far ♪

1133
01:11:14.854 --> 01:11:17.774
♪ Never thought it would get this far
Been around... ♪

1134
01:11:17.857 --> 01:11:19.942
Okay, can we just double that, then?

1135
01:11:20.651 --> 01:11:22.653
-Double that, I think it's cool.
-Cool.

1136
01:11:22.737 --> 01:11:25.698
[playing slow melody]

1137
01:11:30.369 --> 01:11:34.081
[Shawn on recording]
♪ You're the only person ♪

1138
01:11:34.165 --> 01:11:37.627
♪ I keep coming back to ♪

1139
01:11:41.339 --> 01:11:43.758
♪ It's always been you
It's always been you ♪

1140
01:11:43.841 --> 01:11:46.177
♪ Yeah, yeah! ♪

1141
01:11:46.886 --> 01:11:48.513
[song continues playing]

1142
01:11:48.596 --> 01:11:50.848
♪ It's always been you
It's always been you ♪

1143
01:11:59.607 --> 01:12:01.943
♪ It's always been you! ♪

1144
01:12:02.610 --> 01:12:05.071
I'm really excited
to sing these songs on tour.

1145
01:12:05.154 --> 01:12:08.282
All this stuff is so playable,
in the best way.

1146
01:12:08.908 --> 01:12:11.035
I want another "Do you know" to come in...

1147
01:12:11.828 --> 01:12:13.246
behind it there, like...

1148
01:12:13.329 --> 01:12:15.832
And then another third one
to come in there,

1149
01:12:15.915 --> 01:12:17.375
like, kind of, a little rise.

1150
01:12:17.458 --> 01:12:19.335
[gentle piano music]

1151
01:12:19.418 --> 01:12:22.505
When you start an album,
you don't really know what to expect.

1152
01:12:22.588 --> 01:12:25.299
So you just have to dive in
and see what happens.

1153
01:12:25.383 --> 01:12:29.178
[playing bittersweet melody]

1154
01:12:38.062 --> 01:12:41.732
♪ I wonder what it's like to be... ♪

1155
01:12:41.816 --> 01:12:44.860
[indistinct]

1156
01:12:44.944 --> 01:12:47.071
♪ I wonder ♪

1157
01:12:48.531 --> 01:12:50.533
♪ I wonder ♪

1158
01:12:52.493 --> 01:12:55.997
♪ I wonder
What it's like to be my friends ♪

1159
01:12:56.080 --> 01:12:59.333
♪ I hope that they don't think
That I'll forget about them ♪

1160
01:12:59.417 --> 01:13:02.628
♪ I wonder
Why it's so hard to choose ♪

1161
01:13:03.212 --> 01:13:04.422
♪ I should go to sleep ♪

1162
01:13:04.505 --> 01:13:06.340
♪ I think too much ♪

1163
01:13:06.424 --> 01:13:10.595
♪ Right before I close my eyes
The only... ♪

1164
01:13:10.678 --> 01:13:12.847
Some sort of little thing
in the back there.

1165
01:13:12.930 --> 01:13:16.767
♪ Been dreaming 
That you feel it, too ♪

1166
01:13:16.851 --> 01:13:21.022
♪ I wonder
What it's like to be loved by you ♪

1167
01:13:21.105 --> 01:13:23.107
[Scott] Yeah.

1168
01:13:23.190 --> 01:13:24.984
[Shawn vocalizing on recording]

1169
01:13:25.067 --> 01:13:27.612
-You felt that there?
-Little pause? Yeah.

1170
01:13:27.695 --> 01:13:29.238
[song continues playing]

1171
01:13:29.322 --> 01:13:30.323
Hear it now.

1172
01:13:35.369 --> 01:13:37.246
How are the horns sounding right now?

1173
01:13:37.330 --> 01:13:38.873
[song continues playing]

1174
01:13:38.956 --> 01:13:40.750
[emotional drum roll]

1175
01:13:40.833 --> 01:13:44.712
[instrumental song section soaring]

1176
01:13:52.887 --> 01:13:55.139
[on recording]
♪ I wonder when it starts... ♪

1177
01:13:57.433 --> 01:13:59.435
[women cheering]

1178
01:14:04.398 --> 01:14:06.400
[men talking indistinctly]

1179
01:14:08.944 --> 01:14:09.779
[woman laughs]

1180
01:14:09.862 --> 01:14:11.489
Is this how we always assembled?

1181
01:14:11.572 --> 01:14:13.240
-It's our thing.
-Okay, cool.

1182
01:14:13.324 --> 01:14:14.283
[man 1] Good times.

1183
01:14:14.367 --> 01:14:15.326
It's our last show.

1184
01:14:15.409 --> 01:14:18.454
-It's our last show.
-[man 2] And it's sold out.

1185
01:14:18.537 --> 01:14:19.497
Sold out, baby.

1186
01:14:19.580 --> 01:14:21.666
[Shawn] Oh, ho!

1187
01:14:23.334 --> 01:14:25.127
Why do you look so cool?

1188
01:14:26.462 --> 01:14:28.172
-[Aaliyah] How are you?
-Fine!

1189
01:14:28.255 --> 01:14:29.465
-Hey!
-How you feeling?

1190
01:14:29.548 --> 01:14:31.217
-How's it going?
-Mom on FaceTime?

1191
01:14:31.300 --> 01:14:32.176
-She is.
-Hi, Mom!

1192
01:14:32.259 --> 01:14:33.427
I'll flip it around.

1193
01:14:33.511 --> 01:14:35.304
[Shawn] A hundred and five shows...

1194
01:14:35.388 --> 01:14:37.890
The last year of my life
has been this tour, and...

1195
01:14:38.391 --> 01:14:39.684
it's bittersweet.

1196
01:14:41.143 --> 01:14:43.396
It's more sweet than bitter, to be honest.

1197
01:14:43.479 --> 01:14:46.607
This makes me so happy,
when I come into the venue,

1198
01:14:46.691 --> 01:14:48.818
and it's been weeks,
and all of a sudden,

1199
01:14:48.901 --> 01:14:52.154
the "Manny" thing pops up,
and I'm like, "He's coming to town."

1200
01:14:53.322 --> 01:14:56.409
["Gimme Shelter"
by The Rolling Stones playing]

1201
01:14:58.035 --> 01:15:00.663
[indistinct chatter]

1202
01:15:10.923 --> 01:15:13.551
♪ Ooh, a storm is threatening ♪

1203
01:15:14.176 --> 01:15:17.138
♪ My very life today ♪

1204
01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:21.726
♪ If I don't get some shelter ♪

1205
01:15:22.601 --> 01:15:25.229
♪ Ooh, yeah, I'm gonna fade away ♪

1206
01:15:26.272 --> 01:15:29.275
♪ War, children ♪

1207
01:15:29.900 --> 01:15:31.235
♪ It's just a shot away ♪

1208
01:15:31.318 --> 01:15:32.737
-Hey, bro.
-Hey, brother.

1209
01:15:32.820 --> 01:15:34.029
[speaking indistinctly]

1210
01:15:37.616 --> 01:15:39.952
[Shawn] At the end of this tour,
I'm realizing

1211
01:15:40.035 --> 01:15:42.913
this is something
I want to do for the rest of my life.

1212
01:15:42.997 --> 01:15:44.540
[audience cheering]

1213
01:15:44.623 --> 01:15:47.835
How do you get to the end
of a very, very intense year...

1214
01:15:48.919 --> 01:15:50.588
and want to do it all over again?

1215
01:15:56.510 --> 01:15:57.887
At the end of this tour,

1216
01:15:57.970 --> 01:16:01.432
I wish I had some profound thing
to say about all this, but...

1217
01:16:04.393 --> 01:16:05.770
you know what the truth is?

1218
01:16:07.521 --> 01:16:10.858
You walk up on the stage
and you look around and you think...

1219
01:16:11.734 --> 01:16:13.778
"I'm just a guy who really loves music.

1220
01:16:14.820 --> 01:16:15.696
Time to let go."

1221
01:16:15.780 --> 01:16:16.906
New York!

1222
01:16:16.989 --> 01:16:18.741
[playing "In My Blood"]

1223
01:16:24.246 --> 01:16:28.709
♪ It isn't in my blood ♪

1224
01:16:28.793 --> 01:16:30.836
♪ Yeah ♪

1225
01:16:30.920 --> 01:16:32.922
♪ I need somebody now ♪

1226
01:16:34.340 --> 01:16:37.176
♪ I need somebody now ♪

